N2  - ABSTRACTThe fling‐step is a result of the permanent tectonic offset of the ground in the near‐fault regions of large earthquakes. Ground motions containing the fling typically feature a one‐sided pulse in the velocity and a non‐zero permanent displacement (PD) at the end of shaking. Generally, the information regarding PD is not available in many worldwide databases due to the presence of various errors, as well as the limitations of current practices in eliminating the errors that are contained
